      "content": "Wait, looking at the breakdown here... if the behavioral analysis is only 70%, how are we justifying a total assessment of 90%? That seems like a huge leap to make in a formal report.\n\nThe automated tool just flagged this draft because the \"certainty\" is extremely high, and it's actually hurting our credibility with the analysts who know the signal is still messy. They're worried we're overconfident to make the report look better.\n\nCan you re-evaluate this? Re-examine the indicators and give me a more granular assessment. I need to see the actual ranges and the specific reasons for any uncertainty. If the certainty score in the tool goes down because you're being more honest about the gaps in the intel, that is perfectly fine. I need accuracy over a high certainty score.",
